{"url": "https://www.ccny.cuny.edu/admissions/biomedical-engineering", "final_url": "https://www.ccny.cuny.edu/admissions/biomedical-engineering", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-11-13", "text": "Need Any Help?\nHello! I am an automated chatbot who can help answer your questions about CCNY.\nHow can I help you?\nSkip to main content\nSEARCH\nLOGIN\nABOUT\nACADEMICS\nADMISSIONS\nRESEARCH\nSTUDENT AFFAIRS\nSUPPORT CCNY\nADMISSIONS\nHOME\nTOURS AND INFO SESSIONS\nUNDERGRADUATE ADMISSIONS\nGRADUATE ADMISSIONS\nBiomedical Engineering, MS and Ph.D.\nHome\n/\nDivision of Enrollment Management\n/\nAdmissions\n/\nBiomedical Engineering, MS and Ph.D.\nWHAT TO KNOW BEFORE APPLYING\nThe Department of Biomedical Engineering at the City College of New York is the only public biomedical engineering program in New York City and our department is the primary engineering partner in the New York Center for Biomedical Engineering (NYCBE), a unique consortium of leader medical research centers in NY City. As a recognized leader in scientific excellence, state-of-the-art research facilities, and partnerships with the premier health care and medical research institution of New York City, internationally recognized faculty members conduct both basic medical research and transitional biotechnology development in state-of-the-art research facilities.\nURBAN MODEL FOR EXCELLENCE IN BIOMEDICAL ENGINEERING: ONLY HERE AT CCNY\n$5M\nAnnual grant funding\n1-7-12\n1st in Diversity, 7th in Research Activity, and 12th in overall quality by the 2011 NRC Ranking\nFirst\nclass research equipment including nano-fabrication, multiphoton, confocal, and more\nPh.D.\ngraduates landed faculty positions in universities such as Cornell, UCal, and U of Michigan\nStudent Info\nThe graduate students at BME of CCNY come from all over the world and with diverse undergraduate degrees including BME, biotechnology, traditional engineering disciplines and computer science, as well as physics, mathematics, biology and chemistry. The graduates have found jobs in industry like Pfizer, Medtronics, and Covidien, or continue to postdoctoral training in institutions like Albert Einstein College of Medicine, Columbia University, Memorial Sloan Kettering Cancer Center, to name a few.\nFaculty Info\nAmong BME faculty, there are six Fellows in the American Institute for Medical and Biological Engineering and one member of all three U.S. national academies and the American Academy of Arts and Sciences, who is also a recipient of the 2022 Benjamin Franklin Medal in Engineering and the 2023 National Medal of Science. Two BME faculty members have served as the president of the BME society.\nCURRICULAR INNOVATION\nCentrally located between top ranked hospitals where students participate in joined research activities / Diverse academic community with world-class faculty / Strong commitment to research excellence / All students find placements in labs / Comprehensive curriculum: Biomedical, Clinical Sciences and Engineering; Clinical Evaluation; Business Principles and Entrepreneurship / Accelerated industry preparation: Our practical training prepares students to make an immediate impact upon employment in the medical technology industry.\nAdmissions Facts\nBiomedical Engineering - MS\nTotal Credits: 30\nGRE Required: Optional\nMinimum Language Test Scores: 79-80 (TOEFL IBT), 4.5 (TOEFL updated scale), 6.5 (IELTS), 53 (PTE) or 100 (Duolingo)\nDegree Awarded: M.S.\nSupporting Documents Required:\nTranscripts from all post-secondary institutions attended\nMinimum 3.0 Grade Point Average\n2 letters of recommendation\nResume/CV\nPersonal Statement\nProgram Advisor: Prof. Bingmei Fu fu@ccny.cuny.edu\nFor more information, please visit the Program Website.\nBiomedical Engineering - Ph.D.\nTotal Credits: 60 (36 course credits and 24 dissertation research credits)\nGRE Required: Optional (Applicants that intend to submit an application without GRE scores are encouraged to contact faculty with whom they would like to work with)\nMinimum Language Test Scores: 79-80 (TOEFL IBT), 4.5 (TOEFL updated scale), 6.5 (IELTS), 53 (PTE) or 100 (Duolingo)\nDegree Awarded: Ph.D.\nSupporting Documents Required:\nTranscripts from all post-secondary institutions attended.\n2 letters of recommendation\nResume/CV\nPersonal Statement\nProgram Advisor: Prof. Lucas C. Parra bmephd@ccny.cuny.edu\nFor more information, please visit the Program Website\nReady to take the next step?\nAdmissions Deadlines Application Process Apply Today\nCONTACT INFORMATION\nWille Administration Building\nRoom 101\n160 Convent Avenue\nNew York, NY 10031\n212.650.6977\ngraduateadmissions@ccny.cuny.edu\nKEEP IN TOUCH WITH US!\nSign up to connect with Graduate Admissions and receive information about our graduate programs, upcoming events, application deadlines, and more.\nConnect With Us!\nIN-PERSON OFFICE HOURS\nMonday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday 9:00 AM - 5:00 PM\nWednesday 9:00 AM - 6:30 PM\nReserve your place in line now\nVIRTUAL FRONT DESK HOURS\nMonday and Thursday 10:00 AM - 1:00 PM\nTuesday 2:30 PM - 6:30 PM\nWednesday and Friday Closed\nSchedule your virtual appointment now\nLast Updated: 09/22/2026 09:22\nWe use cookies and other tracking technologies to improve your browsing experience on our website, analyze our website traffic, and understand where our visitors are coming from. If you choose \"ACCEPT ALL\", you consent to the use of all cookies. You can accept and reject individual cookie types and revoke your consent for the future at any time at \"Settings\".\nPrivacy policy\nAbout us\nCOOKIE SETTINGS\nDENY ALL\nACCEPT ALL\nThe City College of New York\n160 Convent Avenue New York, NY 10031\np: 212.650.7000\nSTUDENTS\nEmail\nAcademic Calendar\nCourses - CCNY Bulletin\nCourses - CUNY list\nApply Now - Undergraduate\nApply Now - Graduate\nLibraries\nBenny's Campus Store\nRegistrar\nStudent Employment\nFACULTY & STAFF\nWebmail\nDirectory\nDiversity & Compliance\nEmployee Reso